      "body": "Co-authored-by: Codex\r\n\r\n## AI Disclosure\r\nCodex was used to help read and write code, and to write unit tests.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFixes #61215.\r\n\r\nIf the `<think>` block is the last token in the model prompt template, it returns 501 because /v1/systemone requires the first token to be the answer. Thinking models instead reply with thoughts that are noise when converted to probabilities expecting an answer.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n\r\nFixes issue linked above. Before, thinking-only models would return noise rather than a proper probability.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n\r\nAdded a unit test, and locally verified with the original reproduction steps that the issue no longer occurs.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n\r\nThis PR mainly detects qwen thinking-only checkpoints, using the <think> block in their prompt. If it is not present, then other thinking-only models will encounter similar issues.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\r\n---\r\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63509?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith